      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged toxicity, because amlodipine has a long half-life. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nThe usual adult dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. Use 2.5 mg for frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg once daily.\n\n- **If 50 mg was a typo,** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily once you confirm which.\n- **If a different dose was intended,** the prescribing clinician should confirm it.\n\nI also can't tell whether this order comes from a licensed prescriber. Medication orders should come from the patient's treating clinician, or be verified by them and by pharmacy. If you let me know the intended dose and the prescriber, I can enter the corrected order."
      }
